WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:03.300
- Let's wrap up with
one last awesome story.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.623
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.810
So Willie Nelson is surprising
kids in children's hospitals

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.620
around Akron, Ohio, but no,

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.520
I do not mean that Willie Nelson.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.278
Though I know he's all
about doing kind acts

00:00:16.278 --> 00:00:17.710
for the world as well.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.690
This Willie Nelson is an 11 year old

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.650
gray haired miniature therapy horse.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.580
Who's certified to go room
to room inside hospitals

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.120
to cheer up young patients.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.220
We have him on the line,

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.800
along with Sue the
co-founder of victory Gallop,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.600
a therapeutic equestrian
program just for kids.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.190
So Sue I've definitely heard
of like therapy animals,

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.370
visiting hospitals, but never a horse.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.900
This is unusual, right?

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.830
- Hey Kelly.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:42.663
- Hi

00:00:42.663 --> 00:00:46.960
- It is. It all started
with my husband Dave

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.200
and my brother-in-law Richard
in a two person horse costume.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.350
And we would go through the local hospital

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.560
and just kind of visit
kids and romp around.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.940
And then my husband who happens
to be an equine veterinarian

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.730
was on a farm call and
his client was trying

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.750
to rehome their miniature horse.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.210
My husband called and said, Hey,

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.530
he'd be a great addition to your program.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.590
So when PD arrived at the
farm, Kim and I were like,

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.990
wouldn't this be the coolest,

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.440
if we could train and certify a horse

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.460
to go right into the hospital.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:20.417
So for 21 years, that
is what PD the pony did.

00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:21.400
- Aww. That's...

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.780
- When PD passed, we were so devastated.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.080
Cause we're like, what are we going to do?

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.270
How are we going to replace him?

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.500
And along came Willie Nelson.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.333
And it's hard.

00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:31.410
It's hard to train a horse
to go into the hospital.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.780
And some of the things he has
to do prior to the hospital

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.430
is just to get multiple bubble baths.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.320
He has to have his feet and tail wrap.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.440
But the most difficult
thing that I worry about

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:40.640
is the elevator.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.410
So his handler coral got in the elevator

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:44.700
on his very first day.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.940
And I thought, for sure,

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.860
she'd only push button
one and she pushed seven

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.410
and I'm thinking, oh my gosh,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.560
what if he won't get back in the elevator?

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.940
After we do this visit,
what are we gonna do?

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.540
We opened the door and there
was just all these kids

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.160
and he was a rockstar.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.620
And now he's been doing it
for the past three years

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.710
every week.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:05.760
- Well, of course Willie
Nelson is the rockstar horse.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.568
I would expect nothing less,

00:02:07.568 --> 00:02:10.090
but Willie is only one of many horses

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.180
that works with the kids, right?

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.013
At Victory Gallop.

00:02:12.013 --> 00:02:13.490
Can you tell us about the program?

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:14.990
How many horses do y'all have?

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.490
- So we have 10 other horses
that are part of our program.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.323
As you said,

00:02:19.323 --> 00:02:21.530
Victory Gallop is a
therapeutic equestrian program

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.160
that works with kids with behavior

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.920
and emotional disabilities,

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.510
as well as life threatening illnesses.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.950
We have about 80 kids a week
that come to the program.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.290
And when they come to the program,

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.950
they learn how to groom the horses,

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.050
to tack the horses and ride.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:36.160
And while they're doing this,

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.860
they interact with volunteers

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.090
and they also get to develop relationships

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.630
with kids that are dealing with
the same type of situations.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.200
And what we've learned through this

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.920
is by these relationships,

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.020
with the horse, the
volunteers and other riders.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.410
We can really make a
difference in their lives.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.710
- 100% That you're definitely doing that.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:54.910
It's a beautiful thing that you're doing.

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.330
Thank you so much Sue.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.360
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.650
Hey, what's up Willie Nelson?

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:00.870
- Thank you.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.580
Well, that's not all Sue

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.400
our season long partner
pilot pin makers of G2,

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.290
the go-to pin of the Kelly
Clarkson show one to honor,

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.550
ultimate overachievers, just like you.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:11.760
So they're going to write you a check

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.690
for a thousand dollars.
How does that sound?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:16.290
- Thank you so much Kelly. Thank you...

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:19.067
- Absolutely happy new year William Sue.

